  {
    "label": "figure_title",
    "text": "Figure 1. Spatial ordinal analysis on oscillator networks. (a) Schematic representation of a network, where each grey dot represents a node or an oscillator and the black lines represent the connections. (b) Example of spatiotemporal dynamics in oscillator networks. Here the phase is plotted in colour-code, with time in the horizontal axis and node position in the vertical axis. As time evolves, the phase pattern changes due to the interactions in the network. (c) Snapshot of phase pattern for a specific time. We analyze the phase pattern of consecutive nodes with overlapping windows using circular distance. (d) We characterize the phase patterns with these 13 ordinal patterns. The patterns with equal phase are analyzed under a specific threshold σ. After obtaining the probability of each pattern, we then evaluate the permutation entropy, given by Eq. (1). This procedure is performed for each timestep.",
